    "observation": "The entire 1320 by 1080 native raster was opened once. All four labeled panels, right-hand x-axis labels and bottommost circle/annulus boundaries are visible, not clipped. Panel a shades the fourth quadrant to the right of the y-axis and below the x-axis, with solid bounding axes. Panel b shows a solid rectangle with x endpoints 3 and 5 and y endpoints 1 and 4. Panel c shades the right half of a circle centered at O, with a solid vertical diameter and the positive x-intercept labeled 4. Panel d shades the full annulus centered at O; its inner and outer positive x-intercepts are labeled 4 and 6 and both circles are solid. Unit 1 labels distinguish the scales. This is a direct visual observation, not a reused figure-review PASS; the provided native render is reused and current seed SVG bytes were independently hashed."
