  "independent_solutions": [
    {
      "source_number": "131",
      "solution": "For (0,0), 2x+3y=0>-1 and x^2+y^2=0<=2: yes. For (-1,0.5), the values are -0.5>-1 and 1.25<=2: yes. For (1,-1), the values are -1 and 2: the strict first inequality fails despite satisfying the second boundary, so no. For (1/3,1), the values are 11/3>-1 and 10/9<=2: yes. Complete membership sequence: yes, yes, no, yes."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "132",
      "solution": "Rewrite both conditions as -4<=y-x<=4. A(0,5) gives 5: outside. B(-1,3) gives 4: included on the upper boundary. C(-20,20) gives 40: outside. D(100,102) gives 2: inside. Complete membership sequence: no, yes, no, yes."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "133",
      "solution": "a: the closed fourth quadrant, x>=0 and y<=0, including both bounding axis rays and O. b: the unbounded region right of x=2 and below y=-1, including both boundary rays and their corner (2,-1). c: [2,4.5) times [1,5], a rectangle with left, top and bottom boundaries included except for their endpoints at x=4.5; the entire right boundary and both right corners are excluded. d: (-1,2) times (-4,-1), an open rectangle with all edges and all four corners excluded. These describe the complete requested shading, not just isolated vertices."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "134",
      "solution": "a: 2x+6<=y<=-2x+6 requires x<=0; a closed left-opening wedge with vertex (0,6), unbounded to the left, including its two rays. b: |x|+2<=y<=5, so -3<=x<=3; the closed triangle has vertices (-3,5),(0,2),(3,5). c: use the supplied modern erratum identity directly: y-3x-6<=0 gives y<=3x+6; 2y-6x+3>=0 gives y>=3x-3/2. This is the closed strip between two parallel slope-3 lines, unbounded in x. d: 0<=y<=min(2-x,x+2)=2-|x|; the closed triangle has vertices (-2,0),(0,2),(2,0). No source re-audit was performed."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "135",
      "solution": "a: the closed upper half-disk centered at O with radius sqrt(0.64)=0.8, including its horizontal diameter. b: the closed annulus centered at O with inner radius 2 and outer radius 4. c: the intersection of the closed radius-4 disk and the half-plane x+y>=4; the closed small circular cap lies above the chord through (0,4) and (4,0), bounded by that chord and the minor first-quadrant circular arc. It includes the chord, arc and both endpoints, but excludes O. d: x^2<=y<=4 implies -2<=x<=2; the closed region between the parabola y=x^2 and horizontal line y=4, meeting at (-2,4),(2,4), includes both curves."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "136",
      "solution": "Using only the seed prose and the actually opened modern figure 25: a: {x>=0,y<=0}; b: {3<=x<=5,1<=y<=4}; c: {x^2+y^2<=16,x>=0}; d: {16<=x^2+y^2<=36}. All boundaries are included because the relevant axes, rectangle edges and circles are solid. Four panels form one seed with four complete graph-to-system tasks; the visible plotting windows do not add finite bounds to panel a."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "137",
      "solution": "Use the ordinary constant-speed school-model interpretation. a: let n,e be nonnegative north/east speeds in km/h. Perpendicular displacements after 4 h give (4n)^2+(4e)^2=24^2, hence n^2+e^2=36. The north team travels 4.8 km farther, hence 4n-4e=4.8 and n-e=1.2. With n=e+1.2, e^2+1.2e-17.28=0=(e-3.6)(e+4.8); nonnegative speeds give e=3.6,n=4.8. Check distances 14.4 and 19.2 km, difference 4.8 and hypotenuse 24. b: let u,v be the respective nonnegative speeds in m/s. (15u)^2+(15v)^2=3^2 gives u^2+v^2=0.04; 6u=8v gives u=(4/3)v. Thus (25/9)v^2=0.04, v=0.12,u=0.16. Check 6u=8v=0.96 m and 15-second displacements 2.4 and 1.8 m with hypotenuse 3. These are independent models, not a merged speed scenario."
    }
  ],
